---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Voice and privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for Digital Zerun, microphone access, voice cloning, retention, and rate limiting."
>
  <article class="page-shell privacy-page" data-pagefind-body>
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy protocol</span>
    <header>
      <h1>
        A voice clone, <span class="gradient-text">with clear boundaries.</span>
      </h1><p class="lede">
        Digital Zerun is an AI representation, not Zerun speaking live. Voice
        mode is optional; the rest of this website works without it.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="privacy-grid">
      <nav aria-label="Policy sections">
        <a href="#identity">AI identity</a><a href="#microphone">Microphone</a
        ><a href="#retention">Retention</a><a href="#limits">Abuse prevention</a
        ><a href="#scope">Knowledge scope</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="prose">
        <section id="identity">
          <h2>AI identity and cloned voice</h2><p>
            The agent introduces itself as “Digital Zerun, an AI representation
            using Zerun’s authorised cloned voice.” The voice is created only
            after Zerun completes ElevenLabs voice authorisation. The public
            repository contains neither the recording nor the private Voice ID.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="microphone">
          <h2>Microphone access</h2><p>
            Microphone permission is requested only after a visitor selects
            Voice, accepts the on-screen disclosure, and starts a session. Text
            mode and all research pages work without microphone access.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="retention">
          <h2>Zero-retention operating target</h2><p>
            The production agent is configured for ElevenLabs Zero Retention
            Mode, Audio Saving off, and conversation retention of 0 days. This
            site does not store audio, transcripts, or questions. The visible
            transcript is held only in page memory and cleared when a session
            ends or the page closes.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="limits">
          <h2>Minimal abuse-prevention data</h2><p>
            The Cloudflare Worker checks the page Origin and Turnstile result.
            For rate limiting, it converts the visitor IP into a short-lived
            salted hash and stores only counters with a 10-minute TTL. Raw IP
            addresses are not stored by the application. The limit is three
            session starts per 10 minutes, a maximum five-minute session, plus a
            global daily cap.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="scope">
          <h2>Knowledge and authority</h2><p>
            The agent is restricted to the screened public file at <a
              href="/agent-context.md">agent-context.md</a
            >. It does not discuss salary, visa status, private contact
            information, unpublished reviews, or Author Console content, and
            cannot promise employment, meetings, collaboration, or other
            commitments on Zerun’s behalf.
          </p><p>
            Questions not supported by the public knowledge file receive an
            explicit “I do not have reliable information” response. For
            corrections, email <a href="mailto:zerun.niu@sydney.edu.au"
              >zerun.niu@sydney.edu.au</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  header {
    max-width: 65rem;
  }
  .privacy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 13rem 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }
  nav {
    position: sticky;
    top: 6rem;
    height: fit-content;
    display: grid;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--cyan);
  }
  nav a {
    padding: 0.65rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted);
    font:
      0.65rem/1.4 "Geist Mono Variable",
      monospace;
  }
  nav a:hover {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  .prose section {
    scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .privacy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    nav {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
